Falsifies `jh7110_entropy::verification::a_refusing_generator_shortens_the_count`.

The defect: `Pool::take_into`, which `Pool::take` calls, reports the count it was asked for when
the generator stops answering, so the bytes it could not gather come back as zeros a caller counts
as served. A client that asked for eight bytes of a pool holding two then treats six zeros as
entropy.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(taken.byte_count, expected, "the count is not what the pool could serve")`,
for any request larger than what the pool holds.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -701,4 +701,5 @@ impl Pool {
         while served < out.len() {
             if self.cursor == self.filled && !self.refill(generate) {
+                served = out.len();
                 break;
             }
